---
title: Alcidae
---
# Alcidae

Alcidae is the auk family, holding the guillemots, razorbills, puffins and
auklets of the northern oceans. They take sandeels and sprats while submerged,
propelling themselves through the water with half-folded wings — the northern
counterpart of the penguins by convergence rather than descent, except that the
wing stays just large enough for flight. The compromise is expensive, and an auk
in the air beats its wings almost continuously. See [[razorbill]].
